id: bound-battlefield
name: Bound Battlefield
uaType: both
prerequisite: 10+ Force or Magic Score
tpCost: 20
type: standard
actionCost: 3
kiCostPerBaseTier: 6
# Only its Ki is followed (the user's ruling): applied when used, "At the start of your turn, you must spend 6(T) Ki
# Points or all of the Squares that you had transformed into Bound Squares stop being Bound Squares" - paid on its own,
# a Stop on the card. Who may enter or leave, the Collision, the Steadfast Check and Defeat are the table's.
sustained: true
upkeepKiPerTier: 6
sphereMagnitude: destructive
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Destructive Sphere of Bound Squares around you: nobody moves in or out. 6(T) KP at the start of each of your turns
  keeps it.
text: >
  Bound Battlefield: You create a barrier around your foes, preventing them from escaping your reach.
  –Ability Type: Technical/Magical
  –Prerequisites: 10+ Force or Magic Score
  –TP Cost: 20
  –KP Cost: 6(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 3 Actions
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: All Squares within a Destructive Sphere AoE (centered on you) become Bound Squares. All Characters who are
  not on Bound Squares cannot use movement to enter Bound Squares and all Characters who are on Bound Squares cannot
  use movement to leave the Bound Squares. In both cases, the movement stops on the last Square they could move through
  and, if it was inflicted by another Character, they suffer from Collision as if they had collided with a Feature with
  a Hardness Rank of 3.

  You cannot use the Bound Battlefield Unique Ability if the Battlefield has any Bound Squares. If, at any point, you
  are not on a Bound Square – all of the Squares that you had transformed into Bound Squares stop being Bound Squares.

  At the start of your turn, you must spend 6(T) Ki Points or all of the Squares that you had transformed into Bound
  Squares stop being Bound Squares.

  If you fail a Steadfast Check or are Defeated, all of the Squares you transformed into Bound Squares stop being Bound
  Squares.
